# o_\ is transpose (B17): it reverses the order of the axes, as in APL
# and J. A matrix's rows become its columns, a 2 3 4 array becomes
# 4 3 2 (element i j k moves to k j i), and a vector or a scalar is
# unchanged. Transposing twice gives the array back.
== SOURCE
m := 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6
a := 2 3 4 r_eshape r_ange 24
o_\ m
s_hape o_\ a
1 s_elect o_\ a
o_\ 1 2 3
o_\ 5
o_\ "abc"
(o_\ o_\ a) m_atch a
== RESULT
1 4
2 5
3 6
4 3 2
1 13
5 17
9 21
1 2 3
5
abc
1
